    "type": "story",
    "provenance": "original",
    "title": {
     "en": "Adding rice sacks"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "A driver carried 345 sacks one day and 289 the next. How many in all?"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "carry",
     "regroup",
     "estimate",
     "nearest hundred"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "To add big numbers, add ones, then tens, then hundreds.\nWhen ones make 10 or more, regroup 10 ones as 1 ten and carry it. 5 + 9 = 14, write 4 and carry 1 ten.\nDo the same for tens: 4 + 8 + 1 = 13, write 3 and carry 1 hundred. Then hundreds: 3 + 2 + 1 = 6. So 345 + 289 = 634.\nEstimating means finding an answer that is close without exact work. Round to the nearest hundred: 345 is about 300 and 289 is about 300, so the answer is about 600.\nCompare the estimate with the exact answer to see if it is sensible. 634 is close to 600."
    }
   },
